---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { wwd } from '../lib/wwd';

// The Privacy page ("Build the Privacy page", docket:v1:task:01M35J0JQ47JH6V004ZFJZDXFN).
// Anyone can take part without giving us anything; signing up is only for
// LVBT's giveaway, at /sign-up, and asks for a first name, an email address
// or phone number, a ZIP code, an age group and (optionally) an Instagram
// handle. Entries come from checking in on /my-week.
// "Finalize the Privacy policy wording" (docket:v1:task:01M35J0JT1968NPPR4TBRBFSS7)
// replaces this draft later — the whole block between the two DRAFT NOTICE
// comments below is what to delete once that happens.

const title = 'Privacy · Week Without Driving Las Vegas';
const description = 'What Week Without Driving Las Vegas collects, why, and when it is deleted.';
const contactEmail = 'wwd@lasvegasfortransit.org';
const contactMailto = `mailto:${contactEmail}`;
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="container-page page-top reading">
    {
      /* DRAFT NOTICE — remove this block, and this comment, once
        "Finalize the Privacy policy wording" is approved. */
    }
    <div
      class="mb-10 flex items-start gap-3 border border-primary bg-primary-container px-5 py-4 text-on-primary-container"
    >
      <span class="mt-0.5 font-bold" aria-hidden="true">&#9888;</span>
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold leading-relaxed">
        Draft: final wording pending review. This page holds the wording from "Build the Privacy
        page" until "Finalize the Privacy policy wording" is approved.
      </p>
    </div>
    {/* END DRAFT NOTICE */}

    <h1 class="page-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-on-surface-variant">
      Last updated: September 23, 2026.
    </p>

    <article class="prose-doc mt-8">
      <p>
        Week Without Driving Las Vegas (lvwwd.org) is run by Las Vegans for Better Transit (LVBT), a
        volunteer nonprofit in Las Vegas. This page explains what information we collect, why, who
        helps us handle it, and when we delete it.
      </p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Anyone can take part in Week Without Driving. You can read every guide, find a bus and
          play bingo without giving us your name, email address or phone number.
        </li>
        <li>
          Signing up is only for LVBT's giveaway. It asks for a few required details and a couple of
          optional ones, and we use them only for Week Without Driving 2026.
        </li>
        <li>
          We delete personal campaign information on November 30, 2026. You can ask us to delete
          yours sooner.
        </li>
        <li>We do not sell your personal information.</li>
        <li>
          LVBT's newsletter is separate. If you choose to join it, it keeps your email address until
          you unsubscribe.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
      <p>
        We only collect personal information if you sign up for LVBT's giveaway, at
        lvwwd.org/sign-up. These are the kinds we collect:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>First name</li>
        <li>Email address or phone number</li>
        <li>ZIP code</li>
        <li>Instagram handle (optional)</li>
        <li>
          Whether you're 18 or older, or 13 to 17 with a parent's or guardian's agreement to the
          giveaway's Official Rules
        </li>
        <li>Whether you'd like LVBT's newsletter (a box we never check for you)</li>
        <li>Your daily check-ins, October 1 to 8</li>
        <li>
          A photo of the day, if you choose to add one on My week, and whether you let LVBT share it
        </li>
        <li>Your reply, if you win the giveaway and we contact you</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        When you sign up. We ask for your first name; an email address or a phone number, so we can
        reach you if you win and send your personal "Open my week" link; and your ZIP code, to
        confirm you live in Southern Nevada and to show where people took part. Your Instagram
        handle is optional: give it and a tag of @lasvegasfortransit counts as a check-in. Signing
        up means agreeing to the Official Rules. If you also tick "Also send me LVBT's newsletter"
        (it's never checked for you), we pass your email address to LVBT's newsletter. See "LVBT's
        newsletter" below.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your check-ins. Each day you tap "Check in for today" on My week, we record that day as an
        entry, up to {wwd.maxEntries} entries for October 1 to 8. Checking in is free: no purchase, upload
        or post is necessary. If you gave an Instagram handle and tag @lasvegasfortransit on a day you
        haven't already checked in, a volunteer records that as your check-in for the day.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your photo, if you add one. "Add a photo of today" on My week is optional and never gives
        you an extra entry. We never publish it unless you separately check the box that lets LVBT
        share it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you win. We keep a record of the draw with the way you entered — your email address,
        phone number or Instagram handle — and your reply when we contact you at{' '}
        <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a>, at the phone
        number you gave, or by Instagram direct message.
      </p>

      <h2>What the site keeps on your device</h2>
      <p>Some things are saved only in your browser, on your phone or computer:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          A sign-in session, so My week remembers you're signed up. One cookie holds a session code;
          a second just says whether this browser is signed in. Neither one is your name or contact
          information by itself. They last until November 30, 2026, or until you sign out.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your bingo card: which squares you marked, and whether you chose the grid or the list.
          This is never sent to us.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we measure use</h2>
      <p>
        We count page visits and actions like signing up with Cloudflare Web Analytics and LVBT's
        own analytics. These counts contain no personal information: no names, email addresses,
        phone numbers or IP addresses. We don't let advertisers or other companies track what you do
        on lvwwd.org across other websites.
      </p>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        Only the LVBT volunteers who run the campaign can see what we collect, on a page that needs
        a sign-in. These companies help us run the site, and they use your information only to do
        that job for us:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Cloudflare hosts the site, stores the sign-up database and any photo you add, checks that
          forms are filled in by people and not bots, and provides Cloudflare Web Analytics.
        </li>
        <li>Resend sends your sign-up confirmation and your "Open my week" link.</li>
        <li>Beehiiv runs LVBT's newsletter, only if you ask to join it.</li>
        <li>
          Instagram, only for tags you post publicly. When you tag @lasvegasfortransit, a volunteer
          sees your post on Instagram and records your handle. If you win by a tag, we message you
          there.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. If you'd still like to tell us not to sell it,
        email <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a> and we'll confirm.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        Anyone can take part in Week Without Driving, at any age. We don't knowingly collect
        information from children under 13, and sign-up doesn't allow it: you must be 13 or older to
        sign up for the giveaway. If you're 13 to 17, your parent or guardian must agree to the
        Official Rules when you sign up. If you think a child under 13 has given us information,
        email <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a> and we'll delete
        it.
      </p>

      <h2>LVBT's newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        LVBT's newsletter is separate from this campaign. If you tick "Also send me LVBT's
        newsletter" or tap "Join the newsletter", we send your email address to Beehiiv, the service
        LVBT uses for its newsletter, and Beehiiv emails you to confirm. We keep a record that you
        asked: the time, the form you used, and a scrambled code made from your address instead of
        the address itself. Because the newsletter belongs to LVBT and not to this campaign, your
        subscription and that record are not deleted on November 30, 2026. You can unsubscribe at
        any time with the link at the bottom of any newsletter email.
      </p>

      <h2>When we delete it</h2>
      <p>
        On November 30, 2026, we delete every first name, email address, phone number, ZIP code,
        Instagram handle, photo, check-in and draw record we hold for this campaign. After that we
        keep only anonymous totals: how many people signed up and checked in each day, and the
        anonymous counts of page visits and actions.
      </p>

      <h2>See, change or delete your information</h2>
      <p>
        To see the information we hold about you, correct it, or delete it before November 30, 2026,
        email <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a>. Tell us the
        email address, phone number or Instagram handle you used. We'll reply within 7 days. You can
        also unsubscribe from LVBT's newsletter at any time with the link at the bottom of any
        newsletter email; that doesn't delete your sign-up.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this page, we change the "Last updated" date at the top and add a short note
        under it saying what changed.
      </p>

      <h2>More</h2>
      <p>
        Read our <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> and the giveaway's{' '}
        <a href="/giveaway/rules">Official Rules</a>. Questions? Email{' '}
        <a href={contactMailto} data-print-url={contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
